Variant Annotation Pipeline

1. Load, clean, transform, filter dataset
    a. Retain variants per columns in dataset:
        i. cohort_filter: Japan, Italy, France, Paris
        ii. exclude_flag: Where not True
    b. Label and retain only frameshift / nonsense / missense variants
2. Initialize `hgvs` and `biopython` packages
    a. Initialize `hgvs` package modules for remote database connection, notation mapping, variant parsing, and variant validation
        i. Get transcript metadata, full transcript sequence for kcnh2
        ii. Get coding sequence from full transcript sequence
        iii. Define variant validation method
    b. Initialize `biopython` package modules for codon and amino acid mappings
        i. Get codon to amino acid mapping
        ii. Determine all possible amino acid to codon mappings
    c. Frameshift variant computation
        i. Traverse left/right of reference amino acid codon to find codon where SNV results in a stop codon
    d. Parse p. notation of variants
    e. Get codon for reference and alternative (where present) amino acid
    f. Determine all possible SNVs for reference amino acid codon
        i. For nonsense variants: Check if stop codon is present in the list
3. Variant notation conversion (backward: p -> c -> g)
    a. Get all c. variant notations mapped to p. variant
    b. Get all g. variant notations mapped to c. variants
4. CADD (PHRED score)
    a. Get all PHRED scores (as JSON) for g. variant notations using API at: https://cadd.gs.washington.edu/api
    b. Compute aggregates for PHRED scores where more than one g. variants exist for a p. variant
5. SpliceAI
    a. Sample score (as JSON): https://spliceai-38-xwkwwwxdwq-uc.a.run.app/spliceai/?hg=38&variant=chr7-150958430-G-T
